# type_bound_clamp -- (repurposed: type_constraint_bound: clamp to an upper bound). Real integer op math.minInt64 (README s10.6).
# Expected output: 100

TypeBoundClamp is project
TypeBoundClamp module examplesTypeBoundClamp
TypeBoundClamp target console
TypeBoundClamp entry main

examplesTypeBoundClamp is module
examplesTypeBoundClamp path examples.typeBoundClamp
examplesTypeBoundClamp exports main
examplesTypeBoundClamp purpose "Compute typeBoundClamp at runtime"
examplesTypeBoundClamp invariant "Result is computed at runtime"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Compute math.minInt64 and print it"
main invariant "Writes exactly one integer line: 100"
main let operandA immutable Int64 150
main let operandB immutable Int64 100
main let harnessName immutable String "type_bound_clamp"
main let harnessExpected immutable Int64 100
main let noopDecoy immutable Int64 0
main let noopName immutable String "type_bound_clamp: real result (not the no-op 0)"
main do calc
main do writeResult
main do noopCheck
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

calc is call
calc in main
calc invokes math.minInt64
calc arg left Int64 operandA
calc arg right Int64 operandB
calc out outValue Int64

writeResult is call
writeResult in main
writeResult invokes test.assertEqualInt64
writeResult arg name String harnessName
writeResult arg expected Int64 harnessExpected
writeResult arg actual Int64 outValue


noopCheck is call
noopCheck in main
noopCheck invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
noopCheck arg name String noopName
noopCheck arg expected Int64 noopDecoy
noopCheck arg actual Int64 outValue

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode